===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker-|id=cut}}
{{ety|en|id=having a small distance|:inh|enm:schort<id:short>|tree=1}}

From {{inh|en|enm|schort}}, {{m|enm|short}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sċeort}}, {{m|ang|sċort|t=short}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skurt}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skurtaz|t=short}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker-}}. {{doublet|en|shirt|skirt|curt}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|short}}, {{m|sco|schort|t=short}}, {{cog|fr|court}}, {{cog|nl|kort}}, {{cog|de|kurz}}, {{cog|goh|scurz|t=short}} (whence {{cog|gmh|schurz}}), {{cog|non|skorta|t=to lack}} (whence {{cog|da|skorte}}), {{cog|sq|shkurt|t=short, brief}}, {{cog|la|curtus|t=shortened, incomplete}} and {{cog|sla-pro|*kortъkъ}}. See more at {{m|en|shirt}}.
